    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on high-leverage spots tonight, headlined by **Gunnar Henderson**, who leads the squad with an elite 82.40 projection. Facing Cavalli, **Gunnar Henderson** benefits from a strong platoon advantage and a leadoff spot that maximizes his run-scoring potential. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (74.56) is our secondary cornerstone; his efficiency is bolstered significantly by a favorable matchup against Bassitt, where his dynamic platoon split and high-order positioning project a productive night. While **Jackson Merrill** draws a difficult assignment against the elite arm of Logan Gilbert (xERA 2.98), his aggressive placement in the leadoff spot and inherent speed keep him in the lineup despite the SP skill penalty, as we prioritize his stolen base upside in our 5x5 construction.\n\nThe decision to bench **Coby Mayo** (44.92) was our most challenging call, as he narrowly missed the cut behind the more efficient floor provided by **Miguel Vargas** and **Josh Jung**. While **Coby Mayo** offers power, his lower projected spot in the lineup today creates a drag on his run-production profile compared to the infield depth we are starting. We are keeping a close eye on **Liam Hicks** (56.32), who maintains a marginal-to-strong outlook against Martinez. Despite the solid matchup, users should monitor the weather for any lingering risk, as his value is tethered to his elevated spot in the order. With **Jordan Westburg** and **Kyle Tucker** currently unavailable, the roster is leaning heavily on the sustained momentum of **Sam Antonacci** (59.41), whose elite xwOBA metrics suggest he is poised to outperform his baseline projection against Taillon.",
